<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    SpotBugs exclusions for brat-core.

    EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 - "may expose internal representation" - is excluded
    deliberately and temporarily. It was the *only* family SpotBugs found when the plugin was
    introduced (2026-08-04), and every hit is the same open design question, already tracked in
    flight-plan.md's Backlog as "Data-class leaves: final, and some as records?": the data classes
    are mutable, hand their interiors out, and it is undecided whether they should become records,
    gain defensive copies, or lose their setters.

    Suppressing it here buys the rest of SpotBugs - null dereferences, resource leaks, bad
    equals/hashCode, and everything else it detects - as a build gate immediately, without
    pre-empting that decision with nine reflexive copyOf calls. Delete this exclusion when the
    Backlog item is settled; if the answer is "records", most of it disappears on its own.

    Note one of the nine was a false positive: SecretsProviderConfig already copies its maps in the
    compact constructor, which SpotBugs cannot see.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
